Teach, guide, supervise, research, and publish;
Write proposals for student and staff development funding;
Conduct research and disseminate findings widely;
Review articles to maintain teaching quality;
Refine curricula to meet market demands;
Develop materials for optimal learning;
Supervise scholars for quality education;
Foster industry and university collaborations;
Establish community knowledge links;
Contribute expertise to committees;
Develop policies for training efficiency;
Serve as an external examiner;
Assess student practical applications;
Provide tutoring and mentorship to students;
Lead program development for excellence.
For Appointment To This Grade, One MUST Have:
An earned Ph.D. or equivalent degree qualification in the relevant field from an accredited university recognized by the OUK Senate;
At least three (3) years of teaching experience as a Senior Lecturer or equivalent and research experience;
A minimum of forty-eight (48) publication points as a Senior Lecturer or equivalent of at least thirty-two (32) should be from refereed scholarly journals;
Supervised a minimum of four (4) postgraduate students to completion, including at least one (1) doctoral student;
Attracted research or development funds as a Senior Lecturer/Senior Research Fellow;
Registered with the relevant professional body (where applicable);
Have attracted research or development funds or educational resources as a Senior Lecturer or its equivalent.
