Duties And Responsibilities
The duties and responsibilities shall include but are not limited to:
Carrying out routine checks on vehicles;
Driving motor vehicle as authorized;
Maintaining work tickets for vehicles assigned;
Ensuring security and safety for the vehicle on and off the road;
Ensuring safety of persons and/or goods in the vehicle;
Maintaining cleanliness of the vehicle;
Detecting and reporting malfunctioning of vehicles;
Maintaining records on repairs and maintenance;
Timely reporting of accidents and follow up of police abstract;
Loading and unloading cargo;
Carrying out basic motor vehicle maintenance services;
Ensure adherence on motor vehicle inspection schedules and compliance to statutory & regulatory requirements;
Keeping up-to-date insurance documents; and
Upholding integrity in fuel utilization, fuel card handling and passenger care.
Requirements For Appointment
For appointment to this grade, one MUST have:
Kenya Certificate of Secondary Education mean grade D (plain) or equivalent qualification;
At least six (6) years’ experience, three (3) of which should have been at the grade of Driver I or its equivalent;
Valid driving license free from any current endorsements and valid for any of the classes of vehicles or plants which the officer is required to drive;
Passed Occupational Trade Test for Drivers Grade III from Kenya Institute of Highway and Building Technology (KIHBT) or Ministry of Roads and Public Works;
First-Aid Refresher Certificate Course lasting not less than one (1) week from St. John Ambulance or Kenya Institute of Highway and Building Technology (KIHBT) or any other recognized institution;
Passed Suitability Test for Drivers Grade III from Kenya Institute of Highway and Building Technology or Ministry of Roads and Public Works;
Valid Certificate of Good Conduct from the Kenya Police Service;
Proficiency in computer applications;
Shown merit and ability as reflected in work performance and results.
